0 60 508 [
[(Here we divide each complex channel in the Fourier analysis)]
[(by its own magnitude to "flatten" the spectrum. The "squelch")]
[(control limits the amplitude boost the algorithm will apply.)]
[(If infinite, you'll get a white spectrum. If less, the louder)]
[(parts of the spectrum will be flattened but the quieter ones)]
[(will only be boosted by the squelch value.)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
